virgl/vtest: no busy wait before inline readback (protocol < 2)

flush_frontbuffer sent TRANSFER_GET, then BUSY_WAIT, and read the busy-wait reply
first - but with protocol 0 the server answers TRANSFER_GET with the pixels at once.
The first 12 bytes of the image were taken as the reply: the frame was shifted 3
pixels left and the last columns showed stale row padding (xlib GLX + virpipe).

--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_winsys.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_winsys.c
@@ -123,7 +123,10 @@
                                  level, stride, layer_stride,
                                  box, size, buf_offset);
 
-   if (flush_front_buffer || vtws->protocol_version >= 2)
+   /* Protocol < 2 returns the data inline, right after TRANSFER_GET, and the
+    * server reads it back synchronously: a busy wait here would read the
+    * first bytes of the pixels as its reply and shift the image. */
+   if (vtws->protocol_version >= 2)
       virgl_vtest_busy_wait(vtws, res->res_handle, VCMD_BUSY_WAIT_FLAG_WAIT);
 
    if (vtws->protocol_version >= 2) {
